' Observed behavior: runs, provider readers, and parallel tools create new virtual threads per task.
' Java divergence: the current stream buffer is unbounded and no deployment-level admission gate exists.
' Target-only design: HTTP and SSE admission, leases, bounded queues, and the 100-run profile are proposals.
' Design reason: virtual threads isolate blocking tasks; leases protect scarce memory and downstream capacity.
' Architecture change: replace three overlapping documents with one capacity-governance model.
@startuml virtual_thread_capacity_overview
title CampusClaw Virtual-Thread Concurrency Management

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontColor #111827
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam ArrowColor #374151

actor "Internal HTTP Client" as client

rectangle "HTTP and SSE Boundary" {
  component "POST Run API\nauthenticate and validate" as post
  component "GET Event API\nSSE or JSON" as event_api
  component "SSE Subscription Gate\nconnection and byte budget" as sse_gate
}

rectangle "Runtime Capacity Boundary" {
  component "Runtime Health Gate\nOPEN / PRESSURE / SHEDDING / DRAINING" as health
  component "Run Capacity Manager\ncount and weighted bytes" as run_gate
  queue "Bounded PendingRun Queue\nitems, bytes, and time" as queue
  component "Virtual-Thread Executor\none new thread per accepted run" as executor
  component "Agent Loop" as loop
}

rectangle "Phase-Local Capacity" {
  component "Model Gate" as model_gate
  component "Tool Gate\nglobal and per-run" as tool_gate
  component "Store Gate" as store_gate
  component "Attachment Gate" as attachment_gate
}

database "RuntimeSessionStore\nauthoritative run state" as store
database "Bounded Run Event Journal\nordered run sequence" as journal
cloud "Model / Tool / Attachment Services" as services

client --> post : create an idempotent run
post --> health : check admission state
health --> run_gate : acquire run lease
run_gate --> queue : wait only within all bounds
run_gate --> store : atomically accept the run
store --> executor : dispatch after acceptance
executor --> loop : create one virtual thread
loop --> model_gate
loop --> tool_gate
loop --> store_gate
loop --> attachment_gate
model_gate --> services
tool_gate --> services
attachment_gate --> services
store_gate --> store
loop --> journal : append typed events

client --> event_api : subscribe or page events
event_api --> sse_gate : acquire subscription lease
sse_gate --> journal : read after Last-Event-ID
journal --> event_api : ordered bounded events

note bottom of executor
  A virtual thread is created for a task,
  then terminates. It is never borrowed,
  returned, preloaded, or reused.
end note

note bottom of run_gate
  Business capacity is limited here.
  Live virtual-thread count is diagnostic,
  not the normal admission control.
end note

note bottom of event_api
  HTTP lifetime, run lifetime, and
  SSE subscription lifetime are separate.
end note
@enduml

